{# THE AREA'S WIDGET LIBRARY SECTION — how this area's dashboard is composed.

   THE DASHBOARD IS COMPOSED, NOT AUTHORED. What an area shows is resolved from
   every installed module's contribution to the area surface, so the library has
   something to compose only once a module contributes to it. The core contributes
   none: it names no module and ships no widget, which is the same rule that keeps
   a module's removal from breaking this page.

   SO THE EMPTY STATE IS THE HONEST STATE HERE, and it is stated rather than
   hidden: an installation with no contributing module reads why the library is
   empty and what would fill it, instead of an empty plate that looks broken. #}
